			"notes": "Fixes startup crashes and translation cache problems.\n\n- Fix the scoreboard mixin on Minecraft 26.1.2, 26.2 and 26.3. This also fixes the startup failure reported with SkyHanni (#3, #4).\n- Fix offline dictionary matches when formatting codes split a phrase or item stat.\n- Apply Shift bypass and translation settings immediately to entity names, the scoreboard and the tab list.\n- Remove separate stale display caches and deduplicate pending component translations.\n- Keep late API responses from repopulating cleared caches or crossing language changes.\n- Cache French and other Latin-script translations, and use locale-independent dictionary keys.\n- Refresh translations after dictionary changes and reload the selected language with `/translator reload`.\n- Preserve nested translation bypasses and retry cache writes after I/O failures.\n- Prevent malformed API keys from exhausting request permits or leaving translations pending.\n- Add regression tests and verify mixin targets against all four supported Minecraft versions during builds.\n- Publish separate Modrinth versions for each Minecraft target instead of marking every jar compatible with all targets.\n\nChoose the jar matching your Minecraft version: 1.21.11, 26.1.2, 26.2 or 26.3. Fabric API and YetAnotherConfigLib are required."
		},
